Drupal 11 compatibility for drupal/media_revisions_ui 2.1.0.

media_revisions_ui has no Drupal 11 release; 2.1.0 declares ^9.3 || ^10. This is
the Project Update Bot's change from https://www.drupal.org/project/media_revisions_ui/issues/3483658
(merge request !7), which adds ^11 to core_version_requirement and to the
package's composer.json drupal/core requirement. Here both become ^10.3 || ^11,
because renderInIsolation() below needs Drupal 10.3+. Plus two fixes in MediaRevisionController
found by drupal-check on Drupal 11.4:
- renderPlain() -> renderInIsolation() (renderPlain is deprecated since 10.3 and
  removed in 12);
- explicit nullable type for the $entity_repository constructor parameter
  (PHP 8.4 deprecation, drupal.org issue #3625648).

NOTE: the maintainers closed that issue as "won't fix" because the module is
obsolete: Drupal core has provided a media revision UI since 10.2 (core issue
#2911977). Prefer uninstalling this module and using core's Revisions tab.

Composer refuses the package on Drupal 11 because drupal.org's metadata says
drupal/core ^9.3 || ^10. composer.json lists it in
extra.drupal-lenient.allowed-list (mglaman/composer-drupal-lenient) so it can be
installed; this patch then makes Drupal enable it.

diff --git a/composer.json b/composer.json
index ed1731e..3235474 100644
--- a/composer.json
+++ b/composer.json
@@ -11,6 +11,6 @@
         "source": "https://git.drupalcode.org/project/media_revisions_ui"
     },
     "require": {
-        "drupal/core": "^9.3 || ^10"
+        "drupal/core": "^10.3 || ^11"
     }
 }
